%% SportsCal Data Flow Diagram
%% Shows how data moves through the system

sequenceDiagram
    participant ESPN as ESPN API
    participant TSDB as TheSportsDB
    participant Jobs as Scheduled Jobs
    participant Redis as Redis Cache
    participant API as REST API (v2025)
    participant iOS as iOS App

    Note over Jobs: Runs every minute

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over ESPN,Redis: Live Score Updates (Every Minute)
        Jobs->>ESPN: GET scoreboard (NBA, NFL, NHL, MLB)
        ESPN-->>Jobs: Scoreboard JSON
        Jobs->>TSDB: GET soccer scores
        TSDB-->>Jobs: Soccer scoreboard
        Jobs->>Jobs: Transform to LiveScore model
        Jobs->>Redis: SET "latestLiveInfo"
        Jobs->>Redis: SET "latestFullLiveInfo"
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over ESPN,Redis: Schedule Updates (Every 6 Hours)
        Jobs->>TSDB: GET schedules per league
        TSDB-->>Jobs: Schedule data
        Jobs->>Jobs: Transform to LiveEvent/Game
        Jobs->>Redis: SET "latestSchedule"
        Jobs->>Redis: SET teams data
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over API,iOS: Client Request Flow
        iOS->>API: GET /v2025/schedules
        Note over API: APIVersionMiddleware adds headers
        API->>Redis: GET "latestSchedule"
        Redis-->>API: LiveScore
        API-->>iOS: JSON + X-API-Version + X-Min-App-Version
        iOS->>iOS: Check version, update cache
        iOS->>iOS: Render in GameViewModel
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 255)
        Note over API,iOS: WebSocket Live Updates
        iOS->>API: Connect /v2025/ws
        loop Every 5 seconds
            API->>Redis: GET "latestLiveInfo"
            Redis-->>API: LiveScore
            API-->>iOS: WebSocket message
            iOS->>iOS: Update UI with live scores
        end
    end
